Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 MAY 04 ACCESSIONED ON  25 MAY 04 at 12 29 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast carcinoma  outside path REMOVED_DATE  Left breast invasive invasive ductal carcinoma  two nodules  DCIS  Positive margins and positive sentinel node biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 04 at 17 16                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm round portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm exposed cavity  The specimen has been oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch denoting the superior aspect  and a long stitch denoting the lateral aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  The exposed cavity is tan pink and overall fairly smooth  with occasional small brown nodules averaging 0 4cm encountered in its wall  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a very firm  white rubbery cut surface with several clips embedded in the wall of the cavity  The cavity is located 0 4cm from the posterior section margin  0 5cm from the anterior resection margin  1 0cm from the lateral resection margin  1 1cm from the medial resection margin with white fibrous tissue extending from the cavity to the medial resection margin  This biopsy cavity is located approximately 1 0cm from the superior aspect of the specimen and 0 6cm from the posterior aspect of the specimen  The tissue away from the cavity is homogenous yellow without focal nodules or masses  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Biopsy cavity with anterior and posterior margins  B  Biopsy cavity with medial resection margin  C  Biopsy cavity with lateral resection margin  D  Small nodule and lateral and deep resection margins  E  Superior  away from biopsy cavity   F  Inferior medial  away from biopsy cavity   G  Inferior resection margin with fibrous tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is explored for lymph nodes  Multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in greatest dimension are encountered  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  H  Four lymph nodes  I  Three lymph nodes  J  Four lymph node candidates  K  Six lymph node candidates  Resident  CHRISTINE GARCIA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  RE EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Breast CTR Surg WAC 240 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  CONNIE ROCHE  NP KENNY C LAI  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 56 year old woman with very dense breast with indeterminate focus of enhancement seen in the medial left breast on MRI  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  DCIS   MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SEE NOTE  Note  Sections of the core biopsy reveal a rare cluster of angulated ducts infiltrating the stroma which are present over an area measuring approximately 0 2cm  Adjacent to the lesion is a 0 3cm cluster of ducts which are expanded by a proliferation of monomorphic ductal cells arranged in a micropapillary pattern lining the duct structures  The morphologic findings are compatible with a diagnosis of invasive tubular carcinoma arising in association with low grade micropapillary ductal carcinoma in situ  To help confirm these diagnoses  we performed level sections and a panel of immunostains on the core biopsy  Multiple level sections show the DCIS to better advantage  An immunostain for keratin REMOVED_DATE shows focal loss of staining in luminal cells and supports the diagnosis of DCIS  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  demonstrate absence of the myoepithelial layer in the infiltrating ducts and supports the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma  Overall  the findings are limited due to limited sampling of the lesion  however  based on morphology and immunohistochemistry  the findings are compatible with well differentiated invasive ductal carcinoma and low grade ductal carcinoma in situ  Dr  David Wilbur has reviewed this case and concurs with the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  aggregate of multiple tan yellow to gray white fibroadipose tissue cores  which are submitted in toto  in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday August 31   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 51 13PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left    Core biopsy  report_end  , Not_reported.
