unostains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show that there is no evidence of vascular invasion  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 25 x 21 x 5cm unoriented modified radical mastectomy specimen  with a 10 x 7 x 3cm axillary tail  which is used to orient the upper outer quadrant  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm disc of skin on the anterior surface  containing an unremarkable nipple and areola  The remainder of the anterior surface of the specimen consists of unremarkable yellow lobulated breast tissue  The posterior margin of the specimen consists of smooth fascia overlying unremarkable yellow lobulated breast tissue  The margins are inked blue anteriorly and black posteriorly  and the specimen is serially sectioned through the posterior margin  There is an ill defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm stellate area of fibrosis in the upper outer quadrant  adjacent to the axillary tail and 2cm from the posterior and 3cm from the anterior margins  The remainder of the breast proper consists of primarily adipose breast tissue peripherally and primarily fibrous breast tissue centrally  with no additional focal lesions detected  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contiguous section  including stellate lesion and closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Contiguous section  including stellate lesion and anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of fibrous tissue in the area of stellate lesion in the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue in inferior lateral quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of superior medial quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from superior medial quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative tissue from central region of breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 biv