Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 28 CLINICAL DATA  An excisional biopsy on REMOVED_DATE showed invasive ductal carcinoma  grade III III with lymphatic invasion and free margins  There was also ductal carcinoma in situ extending to within 0 1cm of one margin  A re excision on REMOVED_DATE showed ductal carcinoma in situ grade III III extending to within 0 4cm of a margin  as well as extensive lymphatic permeation by carcinoma extending to within less than 0 1cm from a margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 41                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 1 006 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with an irregular contour  A REMOVED_DATE x 9 9cm skin ellipse is attached  with an areola which measures 5 8cm in diameter and a nipple which measures 1 3cm in diameter  There is a 4 9cm linear scar located 5 3cm lateral to the nipple  The overlying skin is otherwise externally unremarkable with no evidence of nipple or skin retraction  Externally  the specimen is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm biopsy cavity which is open and in communication with the deep  posterior  margin  The specimen is inked as follows  black intact deep  posterior  margin  blue superior lateral quadrant  orange  superior medial quadrant  green inferior lateral quadrant  yellow inferior medial quadrant  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal that the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm biopsy cavity extends to within 2 5cm of the anterior margin in the superior lateral quadrant and underlies the linear scar noted on the skin ellipse  Radiating in all directions from the biopsy cavity is irregular  firm  white yellow scar tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow  fibrofatty and unremarkable  It is extensively searched for lymph nodes  and none is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Biopsy cavity to adjacent deep margin  C F  Biopsy cavity  G  Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity in superior lateral quadrant  H   Lymph node  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Yes.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Kristina Braaten  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  CLINICAL DATA  56 year old with extensive DCIS and multifocal infiltrating duct carcinoma  11 of 22 lymph nodes positive  now for mastectomy given positive margin  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  SEVERAL FOCI AROUND THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SPANNING  0 6 CM  AND LOCATED   REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN  SEE NOTE   FIBROADENOMA  NOTE  Unequivocal evidence of invasive carcinoma is not identified in this specimen  see prior report MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the axillary portion  The overlying skin measures REMOVED_DATE x 16 0cm with a REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple which is grossly unremarkable  A 6 0cm linear well healed horizontal scar is present at 10 o clock position which reaches up to 6 0cm from the nipple  1cm lateral to the first scar is a second 2 5cm well healed scar present in the upper outer quadrant  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm cavity which is lined by smooth to focally shaggy wall and which contains a blood clot  It lies 0 5cm from the posterior surface and 1cm from the anterior surface and corresponds to the overlying scar at 10 o clock position  A hemorrhagic tract which measures 4 5cm in length is present beneath the second scar and abuts the cavity and the overlying posterior surface  Small foci of orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis is present in and around the cavity and along the hemorrhagic linear tract  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows diffuse fibrous thickening with focal cystic change  No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary portion  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections from the biopsy  including closest to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections from the hemorrhagic linear tract  including closest to the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section from the breast parenchyma where the cavity and the tract abut each other   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma away from the cavity  upper inner quadrant Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , No.
